    <string name="settings_about">About</string>
    <string name="settings_version">Version %1$s</string>
    <string name="settings_about_desc">OpenBrowser for Android manages isolated browser profiles on your phone. Each profile keeps its own cookies, cache, localStorage and IndexedDB, and can override UA, platform, locale, timezone, screen metrics, WebGL, canvas/audio noise, WebRTC policy and proxy.</string>
    <string name="settings_about_limits">Note: the Android build can use the system WebView (Chromium engine) or GeckoView (Firefox engine). Both ship as prebuilt components, so no local Chromium build is required. Chromium mode supports proxies and fingerprint injection; Firefox mode does not support proxies yet. Fingerprint fidelity is still lower than the desktop app, so validate against your own targets.</string>
    <string name="settings_disclaimer">Follow the target site\'s terms of service and local law. This project does not guarantee anonymity or unique fingerprints.</string>

